    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The Lucas-Lehmer test decides whether M_p = 2^p - 1 is prime with only p - 2 modular squarings. This script rediscovers every Mersenne prime with exponent below 1300 -- including M_{521} through M_{1279}, found by Raphael Robinson on the SWAC computer in 1952 -- and plots the exponents, which grow roughly geometrically.">

